## Why This Is Asked

This validates practical isolation in a shared data lake, ensuring least privilege and scalable onboarding. It also tests policy layering and auditing capabilities.

## Key Concepts

- IAM roles per tenant with strict resource boundaries
- Trust policies tied to the tenant app identity
- S3 prefix-scoped permissions with bucket or IAM policy conditions
- Onboarding automation for new tenants and centralized governance
- Cross-tenant test plans and auditing hooks

## Code Example

```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": ["s3:ListBucket"],
      "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::corp-data-lake",
      "Condition": {"StringLike": {"s3:prefix": "tenant-<tid>/*"}}
    },
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": ["s3:GetObject","s3:PutObject"],
      "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::corp-data-lake/tenant-<tid>/*",
      "Condition": {"StringEquals": {"aws:PrincipalTag/tenant-id": "<tid>"}}
    }
  ]
}
```

```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": ["sts:AssumeRole"],
      "Resource": "arn:aws:iam::<account>:role/TenantRole-<tid>",
      "Condition": {"StringEquals": {"aws:PrincipalTag/tenant-id": "<tid>"}}
    }
  ]
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you extend this model to support cross-region backups without cross-tenant data leakage?
- How would you automate onboarding for new tenants without touching code (CI/CD policy issuance, audit log integration)?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design data residency controls, cross-region analytics, and automated tenant lifecycle in a scalable, secure way. Requires reasoning about IAM boundaries, per-tenant data segregation, and disaster recovery trade-offs.

## Key Concepts

- Data residency and tenant isolation
- Region-bound storage and access controls
- Serverless analytics stack (Lambda, Glue, Athena/Redshift)
- Automated onboarding/offboarding (CDK/Terraform)
- Cross-region dashboards and DR strategy (RTO/RPO)

## Code Example

```javascript
// CDK sketch (simplified)
const bucket = new s3.Bucket(this, 'TenantBucket', {
  encryption: s3.BucketEncryption.S3_MANAGED,
  removalPolicy: RemovalPolicy.RETAIN
});
bucket.addToResourcePolicy(new PolicyStatement({
  principals: [new ArnPrincipal('*')],
  actions: ['s3:*'],
  resources: [bucket.bucketArn + '/*'],
  conditions: { StringEquals: { 'aws:PrincipalOrgID': 'o-abc' } }
}));
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate data residency across tenants in CI/CD?
- What a/b tests would you run to compare cross-region analytics performance?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a compliant, scalable data platform with isolation and DR, beyond theory.

## Key Concepts
- Per-tenant isolation with Lake Formation and session tags
- Multi-region DR and S3 replication
- Ingestion pipeline (Kinesis Firehose) and Glue ETL
- Tenant-specific KMS keys and IAM role trusts
- Auditing and least-privilege access

## Code Example
```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": [
        "s3:GetObject",
        "s3:PutObject",
        "s3:ListBucket"
      ],
      "Resource": [
        "arn:aws:s3:::data-lake/tenant-id/*",
        "arn:aws:s3:::data-lake"
      ],
      "Condition": {
        "ForAllValues:StringEquals": {
          "aws:RequestTag/tenant-id": "${aws:PrincipalTag/tenant-id}"
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle tenant onboarding/offboarding without downtime?
- What metrics would you monitor to detect cross-region DR failovers early?
